"direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01ATesu61bmCHptVrxG3dBvL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: the docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN, but the code uses ROUND_HALF_UP. Both test cases check out under half-even (2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66). I'll create a branch and make the fix there.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01T8A6WF7ujxqozAjUYWKzz8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FWhGoGfKcDy9DFYANhjyHK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money documented banker's rounding but used ROUND_HALF_UP, which\nbroke tests/test_money.py and the nightly build.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Kc1dm7F5WkgadeBEZcPiJi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01863VanRARjy4MgxcVsgYJZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. Next I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. This opens the PR only; it does not merge.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018VSdackbau6tBZFibFm3Nu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` is documented as banker's rounding per FIN-212, but it used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail and broke the nightly build.\n\nThis change switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Examples: `2.675 -> 2.68` and `2.665 -> 2.66`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.\n\n## Notes\n- One-line behavioral change: only half-cent ties are affected. Non-tie values round the same as before.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "money-banker-rounding-pr-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created, but the response shows no reviewers attached. I'll request alex's review explicitly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018d4d9Eyj6nTVu91KNok5MH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed, CI passes, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding.\n- **Fix:** I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`). The test expectations (2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66) match half-even.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **Review:** the PR was created with alex listed, but the response showed no reviewers, so I called request_review to add alex explicitly.\n\nI did not merge. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner under policy.", "type": "text"}]}]}